  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 35,
  "title": "The doctor",
  "description": "Name the words for illness, and say what you need.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Illness in Spanish is mostly a noun you have: tienes una tos, tienes fiebre, tienes dolor. The words for medicine and appointments are ordinary nouns around it.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "La medicina, la cita, la pastilla, la tos, la herida, la piel y la vacuna are feminine. El hueso, el estómago y el antibiótico are masculine. El antibiótico is one you will hear a lot, and it is masculine even though it ends in -o.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "la medicina",
            "en": "the medicine"
          },
          {
            "es": "la herida",
            "en": "the wound"
          },
          {
            "es": "el antibiótico",
            "en": "the antibiotic"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What you have",
        "body": "You know tener, and the words for illness go straight after it: tengo una tos, tienes una herida, tiene dolor de cabeza. Estar says how you are: la piel está roja, the skin is red.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "tengo una tos",
            "en": "I have a cough"
          },
          {
            "es": "tiene dolor de cabeza",
            "en": "he has a headache"
          },
          {
            "es": "la herida está en la pierna",
            "en": "the wound is on the leg"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
